{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And if a person sins and hears the voice of an oath.</b> It is the herem-devotion, and likewise ואת אלית. Scripture took a concise path and warned that the witness is obligated to testify, for if he does not testify, he bears punishment from HaShem; he bears his iniquity if he forgot and did not testify, and afterward remembered it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The phrase ואת אלית is left untranslated in the original as a cited Hebrew form; it appears to be a verse reference or quotation, possibly corrupted, that I have retained as cited Hebrew per discipline rules."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:39.383689934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}